    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "# EasyVista ITSM \u2194 Microsoft Sentinel \u2014 CISO Dashboard\n---\n\n## Solution Capabilities\n\nThis solution provides **full bidirectional integration** between Microsoft Sentinel (SecOps) and EasyVista ITSM (IT Service Management).\n\n| Direction | Capability | Automation |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Sentinel \u2192 EasyVista** | Create ITSM tickets from HIGH-CONFIDENCE incidents only (High/Medium severity) | Playbook: `EasyVista-CreateIncident` |\n| **Sentinel \u2192 EasyVista** | Sync incident status changes (New\u2192Open, Active\u2192Investigating, Closed\u2192Resolved) | Playbook: `EasyVista-UpdateTicketStatus` |\n| **Sentinel \u2192 EasyVista** | Close EasyVista ticket when incident resolved (with classification & comments) | Playbook: `EasyVista-CloseTicket` |\n| **EasyVista \u2192 Sentinel** | Sync ticket status back to Sentinel incidents (Open\u2192New, Resolved\u2192Closed) | Playbook: `EasyVista-SyncStatusToSentinel` |\n| **EasyVista \u2192 Sentinel** | Trigger security response actions from ITSM (isolate host, kill process, quarantine) | Playbook: `EasyVista-TriggerResponseActions` |\n| **Bidirectional** | Enrich Sentinel investigations with ticket info (owner, SLA, status, actions) | Playbook: `EasyVista-GetTicketInfo` |\n| **Data Connector** | Ingest tickets, assets, employees, and CIs into Sentinel for analytics | CCF REST API Poller |\n\n### EasyVista Ticket Content (Full Attack Story)\nEvery ticket created from Sentinel includes the **complete attack narrative**, not just a single alert:\n\n- \ud83d\udea8 **Confidence Gate**: Only High/Medium severity incidents are escalated to ITSM\n- \ud83d\udcdd **Full Attack Story**: All correlated alerts with descriptions, providers, and severity\n- \u23f0 **Chronological Timeline**: Events sorted oldest-to-newest as an HTML table\n- \ud83d\udd0d **Root Cause Analysis**: First-alert attribution, kill chain progression, and attack narrative\n- \ud83d\udcbb **Endpoint Telemetry**: Hostname, FQDN, IP address, OS family & version, Azure AD Device ID\n- \ud83d\udc64 **User Context**: Account name, UPN, AAD User ID, SID, account type\n- \ud83c\udfaf **MITRE ATT&CK Mapping**: Tactics + techniques per alert, and overall kill chain\n- \ud83d\udd17 **IOCs**: IP addresses, file hashes (SHA1/SHA256), URLs, and domain names\n- \ud83d\udccb **Recommended Actions**: Immediate response steps for the IT team\n\n### Status Lifecycle Mapping\n```\nSentinel          EasyVista\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500    \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nNew           \u2194    Open\nActive        \u2194    Investigating\nActive        \u2190    Contained\nClosed        \u2194    Resolved\n```\n\n### Low-Confidence Incidents\nIncidents with **Low** or **Informational** severity are NOT sent to EasyVista. They remain in Sentinel with an `EV:Skipped-LowConfidence` tag and a comment explaining why.\n\n---\n\u26a0\ufe0f *Select a tab below to explore operational KPIs and analytics.*"
      },
      "name": "overview"
    },
